WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.969
 Greg, Paul, congratulations.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.337
You've managed to make
it into the third round

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.872
of this competition, and
you are one step closer

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:08.674
to the title of "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.976
and a check for $10,000.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.046
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges,

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:15.915
where you will recreate an
iconic weapon from history.

00:00:15.981 --> 00:00:19.686
That weapon is-- the makraka.

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:25.825
The makraka is a
sickle-shaped weapon

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.327
with its cutting edge on the
inside curve of the blade.

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:31.231
It was notably used
by the Azande tribe,

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:34.500
a dangerous clan that invaded
and conquered central Africa

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.102
in the early 1800s.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.803
With the help of
the makraka, they

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.639
took no prisoners
while defending

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.040
their land and resources.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.275
The sword was often
used in executions

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:46.679
to remove limbs, and decapitate
intruders or enemies.

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:49.382
The Azandes' fatal and
terrorizing use of the makraka

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.318
is highlighted in the game
"The Deadliest Warrior."

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.956
You will have five
days at your home

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.958
forge to accomplish this task.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.894
After those five days, you will
return and present your weapons

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.129
to our panel of expert judges.

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:05.364
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.667
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:08.501
 Good luck to you, man.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.269
 We got this.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:16.309
 Day one here at my home forge,
and I'm ready to get started.

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:17.743
We're going to be building the--

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:18.911
makraka?

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.880
Am I saying it right?

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.215
One of the things I'm
most concerned about

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:24.183
is being able to
present to the judges

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.986
something that's worthy of
using it and testing it,

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:28.054
but I don't know.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.057
It's a strange-looking weapon.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.258
First, I'm going to go
for a Damascus blade.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.094
It's got about 15
layers, I think.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.462
So I'm going to throw
that in the forge

00:01:36.528 --> 00:01:38.298
and bring it up to the
welding temperature.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.099
What I'm hoping to see
when I press this billet

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.567
is that it takes the
weld immediately.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.836
I mean, I don't want
to see any cold spots.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.071 line:7%
I can still see my joints.

00:01:46.171 --> 00:01:48.441 line:7%
I don't like that.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.309 line:0%
Before I go too far,
I'll grind it down

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.444 line:7%
and see what it looks like.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.182
If this doesn't go the way
I planned it, it is garbage.

00:01:57.282 --> 00:01:59.918 line:0%
I'll have to throw it
away and start over.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.086 line:7%
PAUL: Day two.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:02.421 line:0%
The biggest challenges
for today is

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:03.756 line:7%
coming up with a quench tank.

00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:05.091
This one's not going to work.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.059
This one would be fine
for a big, long sword.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.328
It's a big round sword.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.263
So I've had to build
a new quench tank.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:10.796
Perfect.

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:11.731
Oh yeah.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.766
Now I'm in good shape.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.034
So I'm going into
the heat treat.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.603
It's so long.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.605
With my forge, you can't heat
the whole blade at one time.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.440
You have to kind of drift
it in and drift it out,

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:26.779
and it's kind of a chore,
but it's all I have.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.182
Here we go.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.416
It's not hard.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.784
Son of a bitch.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.752
If you don't have a hard
blade, all you've got

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:36.055
is a real pretty piece of
steel that looks like a knife.

00:02:36.121 --> 00:02:40.960
Heat treating makraka, take two.

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.629
That drags pretty hard.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:44.797
It's not hard again.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:45.532
Take three.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.404
God.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.775
I failed not once, not
twice, three times.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.043
Perhaps it's not the steel.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.244
Perhaps it's my oil.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:00.345
So a quick phone
call tells me there's

00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:02.014
quenching oil in Springfield.

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.582
Road trip.

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:05.852
It's an incredible waste of
time, but I've got no choice.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.724 line:0%
 Seems like I got my welds
real good on my billet,

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.126 line:0%
so I'm going to try
forging this blade.

00:03:14.226 --> 00:03:17.063
My plan for today is
to finish my forging.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.098
I really want to
make sure I don't

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.233
draw this blade out too long.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.668
Otherwise my arc
will be too high.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.637
I don't want it to be
too much of a curve.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.839
It's probably as straight
as I'm going to get it.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:29.409
It's pretty vital to me to
get this heat treat going

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:32.144
and see just how this
blade's going to react.

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:34.480
All right, here we go.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.049
I'm looking at my
heat-treating oven.

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:37.583
I know the blade isn't
going to fit in there.

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.151
It's wide enough, but
it's not long enough.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:40.486
I'm going to try the torch.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.221
Oh, I don't think I'm
going to be successful.

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:43.723
I've got to try something.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:48.928
This might be all right.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.062
I don't know.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.430
It looks good.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.365
I'm going to test it.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.137
[bleep]

00:03:58.203 --> 00:03:59.639
That blade broke.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:02.274
Literally, there's no time
to think about the solution.

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:04.743
I'm just going to grab
that piece of leaf spring--

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:05.444
All right.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:06.945
--start forging a blade.

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:08.180
Doesn't that get you?

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.183
Some guy in a poor,
third world country

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.918
can make stuff like this
that will withstand battle.

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:17.223
And I've got $70,000 worth of
equipment, and I can't do it.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.591 line:7%
PAUL: Day four.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.660 line:0%
I had to drive all day
to go get some more oil.

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.662
I got to get this
heat treat right.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:25.964
Moment of truth here.

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:28.333
I sure hope it's hard.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.504
That's the sound I've
been looking for.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.572
My first oil was contaminated.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:36.509
The new oil, it worked just
like it was supposed to.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.811
Thank you.

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:41.147
I've lost way too much time
because of heat treating.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.082
Fit and finish is my forte.

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:45.317
I don't have the
chance to do that now.

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:48.154
I am a little bit of
panic mode because my time

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.421
has dwindled away.

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:50.589
I'm going to have to
beat this thing up.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:54.726
It has to be an
effective weapon.

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:56.829 line:0%
CRAIG: I had to completely
forge another blade.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.732
Now it's day five, and
I've got 20 hours left.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:00.433
That will work.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:01.867
I'm ready to heat treat.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.936
The reason this blade
failed is because of what

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.271
I have to heat treat with.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.805
I know the blade isn't
going to fit in there.

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:09.208
The plan is to leave a
small slit at the bottom

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.843
that the blade will
slide in and out of.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:13.212
Let's give this a shot.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:16.549
It looks nice.

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:19.519
If I don't get this blade heat
treated correctly, I'm done.

00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:24.657
It definitely hardened.

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:25.991
Oh, what a relief.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:27.927
I've got a blade I believe I
can take to the final round.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:31.363
So now I've got to do a little
fitting on my handle material,

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:35.300
but I don't know if I have
enough time to finish.

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:37.736
 Bladesmiths, to see
what kind of lethal damage

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:40.473
your weapon can do, I
will take your makraka

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:43.108
and I'll deliver lethal blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.410
Craig, you're up first.
You ready?

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:45.143
CRAIG: Yes, sir.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.111
 Let's do this.

00:05:46.178 --> 00:05:46.879
 All right.

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:50.350
[music playing]

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.393
CRAIG: That's nasty.

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:01.894
You can mess somebody
up with that thing.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:05.264
 This is one of the lightest
swords I've ever picked up.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:08.300
But the most important
thing, it will kill.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.502
 Thank you.

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.136
 Paul, it's your turn.

00:06:11.236 --> 00:06:13.139
 I'm ready.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.709
[music playing]

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:28.720
 Well, Paul, where
one was speed,

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.858
this is power because
it's a lot heavier.

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:35.027
It dug in deep into
the chest cavity.

00:06:35.093 --> 00:06:38.297
Overall, your makraka will kill.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:39.598
 Thank you.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.233
 Up next, the strength test.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.336
Dave?

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:45.337
 Gentlemen, an
advantage of that sword

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:47.406
was to actually reach
around the shield

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:48.908
hitting the man behind it.

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:51.711
So to test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:53.579
I'm going to strike
these shields four times

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:55.047
with each of your weapons.

00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:58.484
This kind of wood can withstand
extremely brutal force.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.353
So remember, this
is not about what

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.254
your sword does to
the shield, but what

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.622
the shield does to your swords.

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:05.358
Now, Craig, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:06.159
 Yes, sir.
DAVE: OK.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:12.698
[music playing]

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:25.177
All right, I don't see
any nicks or damage.

00:07:25.277 --> 00:07:27.680
The blade's still sharp.

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:28.280
Very nice.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.114
Well done.

00:07:29.214 --> 00:07:30.282
CRAIG: Thank you, sir.

00:07:30.382 --> 00:07:31.417
 Good job.

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:32.218
DAVE: All right.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:33.753
Paul, you're up.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.955
 Let's do this.

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:39.792
[music playing]

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:50.169
DAVE: All right, Paul, I
don't see any blade damage.

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:52.871
The edge is in good shape.

00:07:52.938 --> 00:07:54.840
I like the leather
wrap on the handle.

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:55.975
It's nice.

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:57.510
So all in all, nicely done.

00:07:57.577 --> 00:07:58.677
PAUL: Thank you.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:07:59.912
DAVE: Next up is
the sharpness test.

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:01.714
For that, I'll give
you back to Doug.

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:05.184
 The makraka sword was
used by Azande warriors

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.153
for beheading their prisoners.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.820
To see how sharp
your weapons are,

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:11.224
I'm going to do a mock
beheading over here.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.391
Craig, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:13.226
 Yes, sir.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:14.025
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:08:14.092 --> 00:08:15.127
 All right.

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:19.031
[music playing]

00:08:22.901 --> 00:08:25.971
 Well, Craig, on a vertical
chop, it was easy to control.

00:08:26.071 --> 00:08:29.875
My worry is about on a
horizontal chop or slice

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:32.645
that the weight would
put pressure on my wrist.

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:34.280
No issues whatsoever.

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:37.216
Overall, your blade will cut.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:38.083
 Thank you.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:38.951
 Paul you're up.

00:08:39.018 --> 00:08:39.552
You're ready?

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:40.286
PAUL: Yes, sir.

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:41.353
 Let's do this.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:44.924
[music playing]

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:54.800
 OK, Paul, the
feel of your blade

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:56.435
is a little bit on the
heavy side when you're

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:58.170
doing a horizontal slice.

00:08:58.271 --> 00:09:00.706
It got hung up on
the watermelon,

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:02.308
almost cutting all
the way through them.

00:09:02.374 --> 00:09:06.145
But on the vertical slice, it
just pulls you in and easily

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:08.246
cuts all the way through.

00:09:08.313 --> 00:09:10.382
Your makraka will cut.

00:09:10.482 --> 00:09:11.550
 Thank you.

00:09:11.616 --> 00:09:13.285
 Bladesmiths, in
just five days you've

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:17.423
done some exceptional work, and
your blades perform very well.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:18.858
But in this arena
of competition,

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:21.526
there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:09:21.593 --> 00:09:22.895
and that champion is--

00:09:28.066 --> 00:09:28.534
Craig.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:29.769
Congratulations.

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:32.238
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:33.472
 Thank you, all.

00:09:33.572 --> 00:09:35.641
 Paul, your blade
did not make the cut.

00:09:35.707 --> 00:09:38.477
 Paul, you gave us
a powerful blade,

00:09:38.577 --> 00:09:40.446
but you fell short on sharpness.

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:42.047
The bottom line,
it under-performed

00:09:42.114 --> 00:09:46.652
the watermelons, and for that
reason, we have to let you go.

00:09:46.719 --> 00:09:48.220
 I accomplished
what I wanted to do.

00:09:48.286 --> 00:09:51.489
There are guys on here that
have made thousands of blades

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.192
and didn't make it
as far as I did.

00:09:53.258 --> 00:09:54.159
- Thanks, Paul.
- OK.

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:55.494
 Take care, man.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:56.495
PAUL: The first thing
I do when I get home

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:57.396
is I'm going to take a nap.

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:58.129
It was a hell of a week.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:01.166
I lost 5 pounds.

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:03.802
 Craig, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:06.972
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.440
Congratulations.

00:10:08.507 --> 00:10:09.507
 I'm quite surprised.

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:10.909
I never thought
I'd get this far.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.044
 Why don't you present
your blade to the judges?

00:10:13.111 --> 00:10:14.679
CRAIG: I certainly didn't
walk away with this.

00:10:14.779 --> 00:10:17.016
Paul put up a fight,
but I could come there

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:19.585
with the best-looking thing,
but if it doesn't perform,

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:21.687
then you're out.

